    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/155220641/v5.20.0</id>
    <updated>2026-10-15T18:05:36Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/releases/tag/v5.20.0"/>
    <title>Release v5.20.0</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;Release v5.20.0&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;New Model additions&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Muse Spark Open&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; href=&quot;https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/73884904/674958908-bf34ea27-0edf-4ded-ba6f-905b04096126.png?jwt=REDACTED&quot;&gt;&lt;img width=&quot;2000&quot; height=&quot;1080&quot; alt=&quot;image&quot; src=&quot;https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/73884904/674958908-bf34ea27-0edf-4ded-ba6f-905b04096126.png?jwt=REDACTED&quot; content-type-secured-asset=&quot;image/png&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1080px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Muse Spark Open is a multimodal mixture-of-experts model from Meta that takes text, images, audio, and video as input and generates text. It has 816B total parameters (42B active per token) and a context window of up to 1,048,576 tokens shared across modalities. It is trained for agentic coding tasks such as multi-file editing, debugging, and tool use. Checkpoints are available in BF16 and NVFP4 formats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/muse_spark&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;http://hf.co/blog/meta-muse-spark-open&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Blog Post&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add Muse Spark Open (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5870734437&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/49644&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49644/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49644&quot;&gt;#49644&lt;/a&gt;) by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/guarin/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/guarin&quot;&gt;@guarin&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49644&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49644/hovercard&quot;&gt;#49644&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Ling 3.0&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ling 3.0 Flash is a hybrid Mixture-of-Experts language model from InclusionAI. Its decoder groups five Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) layers with one Multi-head Latent Attention (MLA) layer. The MLA blocks use interleaved rotary embeddings and a head-wise output gate, and the feed-forward blocks combine routed and shared experts. It is natively supported in Transformers as &lt;code&gt;BailingHybridForCausalLM&lt;/code&gt;, so it loads without &lt;code&gt;trust_remote_code=True&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/bailing_hybrid&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Model] Add native Ling 3.0 Flash support (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5772220508&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/49446&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49446/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49446&quot;&gt;#49446&lt;/a&gt;) by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/icavan/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/icavan&quot;&gt;@icavan&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49446&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49446/hovercard&quot;&gt;#49446&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Kolibri1&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kolibri 1 is Aleph Alpha&#39;s mixture-of-experts reasoning model, focused on German and English. Each of its 50 layers routes every token to 6 of 384 experts using sigmoid routing, and adds one shared expert. Four sliding-window attention layers alternate with one full-attention layer, and RoPE is applied only in the sliding-window layers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/kolibri1&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add Kolibri 1 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5778636610&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/49463&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49463/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49463&quot;&gt;#49463&lt;/a&gt;) by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/lucamotz/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/lucamotz&quot;&gt;@lucamotz&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49463&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49463/hovercard&quot;&gt;#49463&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;MiniCPM-V</content>
