  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/155220641/v5.18.0</id>
    <updated>2026-09-30T16:46:27Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/releases/tag/v5.18.0"/>
    <title>Release 5.18.0</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h2&gt;New Model additions&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nemotron 3 Diarization&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; href=&quot;https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/73884904/662347324-fe735cb3-9e5b-43ad-8f60-9dec8425aec7.png?jwt=REDACTED&quot;&gt;&lt;img width=&quot;1680&quot; height=&quot;900&quot; alt=&quot;image&quot; src=&quot;https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/73884904/662347324-fe735cb3-9e5b-43ad-8f60-9dec8425aec7.png?jwt=REDACTED&quot; content-type-secured-asset=&quot;image/png&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 900px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nemotron 3 Diarization is an open-weight streaming speaker diarization model designed to determine &quot;who spoke when&quot; in real-world audio. It supports both streaming and offline inference, handles up to eight speakers, and orders speaker outputs by each speaker&#39;s first arrival in the input audio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The model uses the Arrival-Order Speaker Cache (AOSC) &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/papers/2507.18446&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt; and FIFO queue introduced for Streaming Sortformer &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/papers/2507.18446&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/papers/2409.06656&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. A single checkpoint supports configurable latency profiles, from an 80 ms input buffer to a 30.4 s offline-style buffer, and configurable output frame resolution in multiples of 10 ms. With chunked inference, the maximum audio duration is not limited.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/nemotron3_diarization&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add Nemotron3Diarization (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5555353577&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/49056&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49056/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49056&quot;&gt;#49056&lt;/a&gt;) by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/eustlb/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/eustlb&quot;&gt;@eustlb&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49056&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/49056/hovercard&quot;&gt;#49056&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;NemotronH Omni&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NemotronH Omni is a multimodal reasoning model from NVIDIA that pairs the &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/nemotron_h&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;NemotronH&lt;/a&gt; hybrid&lt;br&gt;
Mamba-Transformer language model with a &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/radio&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;RADIO&lt;/a&gt; vision encoder and an optional Parakeet-based sound encoder.&lt;br&gt;
Image (and video) patches are projected through a RADIO tower and a pixel-shuffle MLP into the language model&#39;s&lt;br&gt;
embedding space at the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;image&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;video&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; context-token positions; audio clips are projected in the same way at&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;audio&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; positions. The result is a single autoregressive model that reasons jointly over text, images, video and&lt;br&gt;
sound.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/nemotron_h_omni&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add support for Nemotron Omni (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4616428476&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/46509&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/46509/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/46509&quot;&gt;#46509&lt;/a&gt;) by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/meatybobby/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/meatybobby&quot;&gt;@meatybobby&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/46509&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/huggingface/transformers/pull/46509/hovercard&quot;&gt;#46509&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;HyperCLOVAX Vision V2&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HyperCLOVAX Vision V2 is a multimodal vision-language model developed by NAVER. It combines the &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/hyperclovax&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;HyperClovaX&lt;/a&gt; language model backbone with a &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/model_doc/qwen2_5_vl&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Qwen2.5-VL&lt;/a&gt; vision encoder. The model supports text, image, and video inputs and is capable of chain-of-thought reasoning via built-in thinking tokens (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;think&amp;gt;...&amp;lt;/think&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt;</content>
